## Elastic shows how to join Claude activity with application traces

Source: Elastic Observability Labs — https://www.elastic.co/observability-labs/blog/ai-agent-observability-claude-platform-opentelemetry
Published: 2026-10-27
Channel: news

Elastic, a platform for searching operational data, documents how to investigate Claude activity alongside application traces. Its October 27 guide uses OpenTelemetry, a standard for exporting telemetry. A span records one operation. Console export supplies platform activity; SDK export adds work inside the application.

For illustration, a slow assistant might spend time in a model request or in a custom tool. Sending both streams helps distinguish those steps. The guide says console export cannot see work that stays inside your process. That requires application instrumentation.

Setup needs a Claude organization administrator, an Elastic trace endpoint and a key allowed to write traces. The guide includes a test-span query to check delivery. Full-content mode includes conversation text; metadata-only mode omits it. Claude export is in public beta. Elastic’s GenAI tab is a technical preview on Serverless and Cloud Hosted 9.6; older versions show key values.

Why it matters: For teams exporting Claude traces: test both platform and application coverage, and choose content retention before enabling export.

